// Legal and help copy, in plain English. Every position here is settled from the law itself (the Acts, regulations,
// regulators' guidance and cases): docs/legal-basis.md is the register, clause by clause, with the sources. A lawyer
// gives it a final read before launch (on the launch checklist), not before each change. Change a rule in the engine
// and the wording here together, and the reverse.
// {{TOKENS}} are filled from Admin → Fees & settings by fillLegal(), so the pages always match the fees charged.
// How bidders pay can be switched in Admin: a paragraph (or Help question, or Help section title) that starts with
// [[transfer]] only shows with no deposit (the default, like Turners); [[deposit]] only with a bidding deposit.

export const TERMS_VERSION_LABEL = "Version 15 November 2026";

export const TERMS: [string, string, string[]][] = [
 ['t-summary','The short version',[
  'Every truck is sold in a <b>live online auction</b>, run by a licensed auctioneer, and sold under the hammer. Super Trucker runs each auction as the owner’s agent. The contract of sale is between you and the owner, and it’s made through us: we run the sale, hold your money in trust and deal with the owner for you. You meet the owner only to view the truck and to collect it.',
  'Every listing has an <b>auction estimate</b>: our opinion of where bidding is likely to end, from recent sales of similar vehicles and what the seller has shown and told us. It’s a guide, not a promise, and the seller’s reserve is never above its low end (section 3).',
  'We’re never at the truck, so see it yourself: <b>view it by appointment</b> where it’s kept (section 5). The owner sends the photos and a walkaround video; we check them against the registration record, the PPSR search and the papers before the listing goes live, and the listing shows what we checked and what came from the owner. Bring a mechanic to your viewing if you like, and ask us anything.',
  'Bid early on the listing, or live in the auction room when the truck is offered. You can withdraw a bid until the hammer falls. When the countdown ends, the highest bid buys it if it meets the reserve. If it doesn’t, the truck is <b>passed in</b>: it isn’t sold and nobody owes anything, and it goes into a later auction. We don’t sell trucks after the auction by private treaty (section 6).',
  '[[deposit]]Registering and bidding are free. To bid you need a verified mobile, a verified ID and a refundable <b>bidding deposit</b>, paid by PayID or bank transfer from an account in your name. The deposit is {{DEPOSIT_RATE}} of the most you want to bid, at least {{DEPOSIT_MIN}}.{{DEPOSIT_ANY}} One deposit covers every vehicle you’re winning, and you can withdraw whatever isn’t holding a bid at any time.',
  '[[transfer]]Registering and bidding are free. To bid you need a verified mobile and a verified ID (a driver licence or passport and a selfie). There’s no deposit and no card, so you can bid while your finance is being arranged.',
  '[[deposit]]If the hammer falls on your bid, you’ve bought the vehicle. The deposit for the price goes towards it straight away, and you pay the balance by PayID or bank transfer within {{PAY_DAYS}} business days. You lose that deposit only if you don’t pay.',
  '[[transfer]]If the hammer falls on your bid, you’ve bought the vehicle: pay the full amount by PayID or bank transfer within {{PAY_DAYS}} business days (your lender can pay it if you’re using finance). If you don’t pay, the sale is cancelled and your account is closed for good.',
  'Fees: a buyer’s premium of {{PREMIUM}} of the price{{PREMIUM_MIN_PART}}, plus GST on the premium{{ADMIN_FEE_PART}}. Nothing is added for transport: you collect the truck where it’s kept. Every price and estimate shows its all-in amount beside it, in the same size. We don’t take cards, so there’s never a surcharge.',
  'Once you’ve paid in full, we lodge the seller’s notice of disposal for them, and you book a time to collect the truck from where it’s kept. We agree the time with the seller, then send you the address and a release code. Putting the registration into your own name is your step, with your state, and it doesn’t hold up your collection.',
  'Trucks are sold <b>as is, where is</b>: in their condition at the fall of the hammer, for collection from where they’re kept. Reports, grades and estimates are a guide only. But the facts in a listing (make, model, year, VIN, odometer reading, GVM, transmission, fuel, listed features, write-off status, finance, visible damage) must be right, and if they’re materially wrong you can claim (section 12). Your rights under the Australian Consumer Law aren’t affected (section 4).',
  'You get clear title: any finance owing is paid out of the sale before the seller is paid. The truck stays in the seller’s hands, and at the seller’s risk, until it’s handed over to you (or until your collection window ends, if you don’t collect in time). We hold your money in trust until the handover is done and your claim window has closed.',
  'There’s no cooling-off period for a sale by auction.',
  'We take payment by PayID and bank transfer only, never cards, cash or cheques, and only into the account shown in your account or on your invoice page. Overdue balances may attract interest at {{LATE_INTEREST}} a year; there are no other late fees.',
  'You collect at a booked time, with whatever the truck needs to be moved safely and legally (section 16). The address comes with your confirmed time.',
  'The listing shows the suburb, not the street, and doesn’t name the owner. We give the address only to a verified member with a viewing or collection we’ve booked. <b>Every sale goes through us</b>: don’t ask an owner to deal direct, and don’t accept if one offers. If you buy a truck we introduced you to from its owner some other way, you owe us our premium (sections 5 and 18).']],
 ['t-agent','1. Who you are dealing with',[
  '{{LEGAL_NAME}} (ABN {{ABN}}) (“Super Trucker”, “we”) runs live online auctions of trucks owned by businesses and private sellers in {{SELL_STATES}}. We act as the owner’s agent under a written agency (consignment) agreement, and our auctions are conducted by a licensed auctioneer we employ. We don’t own the vehicles we sell.',
  'When the auctioneer accepts your bid at the fall of the hammer, a binding contract of sale is made between you and the owner on these terms. We make it for the owner, as their agent. The listing doesn’t name the owner, and the law allows an agent to contract for an owner it doesn’t name; where a state’s law puts the owner’s name on your sale paperwork (Queensland does), it’s there. We take on what you’d otherwise have to chase an owner for: we collect your payment and hold it in trust for the owner until the sale completes, and we’re responsible to you for running the sale, the facts we check (section 3), title (section 9) and every refund these terms promise. If the owner doesn’t complete a sale through no fault of yours, we refund everything you paid.',
  'We hold the licences each state requires for what we do there: {{LICENCES}}. The auctioneer’s name is shown in the live room for the whole auction.',
  'Each listing says whether the seller is a <b>business seller</b> (a business selling a vehicle it owns, such as a fleet or company truck) or a <b>private seller</b> (a person selling their own vehicle).']],
 ['t-location','2. Where vehicles are',[
  'Every vehicle stays where its owner keeps it (their yard, depot or property) until it’s sold, paid for and collected. It isn’t at a Super Trucker yard, and nobody from Super Trucker visits it.',
  'Each listing shows the suburb and state where the vehicle is kept. The street address isn’t published. We give it only to a verified member whose viewing we’ve booked (section 5), and to the buyer once a collection time is confirmed (section 9).',
  'Photos and videos show the vehicle: we remove the location a phone records, and we check they don’t show a street address. An owner’s name or fleet number may be painted on a truck. That doesn’t change who you deal with: every question, offer and sale goes through us (section 18).']],
 ['t-condition','3. Listings, the auction estimate and condition reports',[
  'We’re never at the vehicle. The seller sends the photos and a walkaround video, taken for the listing, and answers our questions in writing. Before a listing goes live, our staff check what the seller sent against itself and the records: the VIN against the photo of the VIN or compliance plate, the registration record and the PPSR search (finance, written-off and stolen status); the build date; the GVM against the compliance plate; the odometer against the seller’s photo of the dash with the ignition on; the transmission, the fuel type and every feature listed against the photos and video; any dash warning lights; whether the video shows it starting and moving under its own power; that the damage the photos and video show is listed; that the photos are of this vehicle; and that nothing in them gives a street address. The listing shows these as checked by Super Trucker. See <a class="blue" href="/listing-promise">How we check listings</a>.',
  'Everything else in a listing comes from the seller and is labelled as theirs: the photos and video themselves, their written declarations (accidents, flood or hail, modifications, previous use, recalls, known faults, service history, keys), their comments, and any report or certificate they supply. We pass it on as the seller gave it. We don’t adopt it as our own statement or check it beyond what we say we check, and the seller is responsible to us for it being true.',
  'The auction estimate is our opinion, made with reasonable care, of where bidding is likely to end. We base it on recent sales of similar vehicles (ours and published results), price guides, and the vehicle’s condition as the seller’s photos, video and declarations show it, and we keep a written record of that basis. It isn’t a valuation, and it isn’t a promise: a vehicle may sell for more or less, or be passed in. The seller’s reserve is never above the estimate’s low end, and the range is never more than 25% wide (or $1,000 for cheaper vehicles). If we change an estimate after a vehicle is listed, the change is shown as a correction.',
  '“Starts and drives” means the seller’s video shows it starting and moving under its own power. It isn’t a road test or a mechanical inspection. “Starts, but doesn’t drive”, “Doesn’t start” and “Not tested” mean what they say: allow for transport.',
  'Corrections: if we find a mistake in a listing, we correct it straight away and show the change, with the date, in “Changes to this listing”. This covers the key facts, the estimate, the title, the description, where it’s kept, the statutory warranty statement, the inspection certificate and the damage list. We tell everyone who has bid on or is watching the vehicle, and a corrected vehicle isn’t offered in the live auction until at least 24 hours after the change. If a correction changes your mind, withdraw your bid (section 6).',
  'Our reports come from the seller’s photos and walkaround video and their written declarations. They are not mechanical, structural, electrical or roadworthy inspections, and they can’t show what the photos and video don’t. Faults may exist that neither we nor the seller know about. That’s what a viewing is for (section 5).',
  'Visual grades describe how the vehicle looks in the seller’s photos and video. They don’t assess mechanical condition. Grade definitions are in the Help centre.',
  'Odometer and hours: the readings come from the seller’s photo of the dash, taken with the ignition on for this listing, so the listing matches the dash. We can’t tell whether the dash shows the vehicle’s true distance (for example after a replaced instrument cluster or engine), so the seller declares in writing whether they know of any reason it may be inaccurate. A listed truck is parked, not worked: the seller may move it a little to keep it in condition, and if the reading goes up by more than 50 km, we correct the listing. The reading is recorded again at the handover.',
  '“Year” means the build year unless the listing says it’s the compliance date. Keys, service books, manuals and accessories are included only if the listing says so. Any remaining manufacturer’s warranty is between you and the manufacturer. Reports supplied by the seller (for example an old roadworthy or a mechanic’s report) are passed on as the seller gave them and aren’t checked or warranted by us.',
  'Used trucks have worked for a living and often need repairs. Satisfy yourself before you bid: view it if you can, read the whole listing, watch the video and ask us any question. If you don’t view it, bid only on what the listing tells you.']],
 ['t-asis','4. As is, where is, and your consumer rights',[
  'Every vehicle is sold as is, where is: in its condition at the fall of the hammer, with any faults that aren’t described, for collection from where it’s kept (the listing shows the suburb). Neither Super Trucker nor the seller promises anything about the vehicle’s mechanical condition, roadworthiness or history beyond the facts we check (section 3), the seller’s written declarations and what these terms say, except where the Australian Consumer Law says otherwise (below).',
  'Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or changes any right you have under the Australian Consumer Law that can’t lawfully be excluded.',
  '<b>A vehicle sold under the hammer is sold by auction</b>, by Super Trucker as the owner’s agent, so it’s a “sale by auction” under the Australian Consumer Law (section 2 of Schedule 2 to the Competition and Consumer Act 2010). The guarantees of clear title, undisturbed possession and no undisclosed securities (sections 51 to 53) apply to every sale. The guarantees of acceptable quality, fitness for purpose and matching the description or sample (sections 54 to 59) don’t apply to sales by auction. That’s the same whether the seller is a private person or a business, and whatever the price: a truck bought to carry goods on public roads is covered by the Australian Consumer Law at any price, and the same rule about auctions applies to it.',
  '<b>Every sale is under the hammer.</b> Outside an auction those quality guarantees can apply to a goods vehicle at any price, which is one reason we don’t sell trucks after the auction by private treaty (section 6).',
  'Whatever the seller is, if a listing is misleading you keep your rights under the Australian Consumer Law, which can’t be excluded, and you can claim under section 12. Any remaining manufacturer’s warranty transfers with the vehicle. You don’t need to buy an extended warranty to have these rights.',
  'Statutory warranty: we sell every vehicle as its owner’s agent, and we never give a statutory warranty or take on a dealer’s duty to repair. Each listing, and the live room while the vehicle is up, says that none applies to the sale. For a truck we sell at auction for its owner, none applies in Queensland (a commercial vehicle, and a vehicle sold on consignment for an owner who isn’t a motor dealer, are both excluded), in New South Wales (a vehicle sold at auction with our notice that the dealer guarantee doesn’t apply) or in Western Australia (the dealer’s duty to repair doesn’t apply to a sale by auction for an owner who isn’t in the vehicle trade). We don’t list a vehicle that would carry one: anywhere, a motor dealer’s own vehicle that a statutory warranty would cover; in Western Australia, a vehicle whose owner bought it to resell.',
  'No cooling-off period applies to a sale by auction: the cooling-off rights for buying a used vehicle from a dealer don’t apply to auctions.']],
 ['t-inspect','5. Viewing by appointment; inspections',[
  '<b>Viewing.</b> You can view a truck before you bid: in person, by appointment, where it’s kept. Ask on the listing and offer up to three times that suit you, up to the day before the auction. Viewings are for verified members (the same checks as bidding), because the owner is told who is coming. We agree a time with the owner and send you the address. No booking, no visit: don’t turn up unannounced, don’t bring anyone we haven’t been told about other than your mechanic, and don’t go back afterwards.',
  'At the viewing: bring photo ID and your booking reference. The owner or their staff show you the truck. Look it over, climb in, start it and hear it run. There’s no road test, and nothing is taken apart. A truck yard is a workplace: wear closed shoes, follow the site’s rules and stay with your host. Nobody from Super Trucker is there. You’re responsible for damage or injury that you or anyone with you cause, except to the extent the owner or we caused it.',
  '<b id="t-intro">Introductions.</b> We introduce you to the truck and its owner so you can decide what to bid. In return you agree, when you book: you won’t make the owner an offer or ask them to deal direct; and if you buy that truck from its owner other than through Super Trucker, while it’s listed or within {{EXCLUSIVITY_DAYS}} days after, you pay us the buyer’s premium we would have earned on the price you paid ({{PREMIUM}} of it, plus GST). That is what we lose when a sale we set up goes around us, and no more. We collect it once: from you or from the owner, who has agreed to the same thing, not both. We keep what you agreed to with your booking.',
  'What an owner tells you at a viewing isn’t part of the listing, and we weren’t there to hear it. If something they say matters to what you’d bid, ask us to confirm it in writing before the auction: we put it to the owner and, if it’s right, add it to the listing for every bidder.',
  'Some owners can’t host viewings (a remote site, a working depot). The listing says so before you bid.',
  'Questions: ask on the listing or call the consultant shown on it. We put it to the owner and answer, and we publish answers that help everyone. If a photo or the video doesn’t show something, ask: we’ll ask the owner for another.',
  'Mechanical inspection: bring your own mechanic to a viewing, or, if you can’t get there and we have a partner mechanic near the truck, order an inspection through the listing or your consultant. The mechanic inspects the vehicle where it’s kept (they may start it, run it and look underneath where they safely can) and emails you a written report with photos. You pay the mechanic for it. We arrange the time with the owner, and you don’t need to be there.',
  'The mechanic is independent of Super Trucker and the seller. Their report is their opinion of the vehicle’s condition on the day, under their own terms, and it says what they could and couldn’t check: without a hoist or a workshop, an inspection where the vehicle is kept can’t find every fault. We may receive a fee from them. A report doesn’t change these terms or the as is, where is basis of sale.',
  'Inspected listings: some sellers have a mechanic inspect the vehicle before it lists. Those listings are marked “Inspected” and the mechanic’s report is available to signed-in members. It describes the vehicle on the day it was inspected; things can change, and you can still order your own inspection.',
  'A viewing or an inspection doesn’t delay the auction, so allow time for it before the vehicle is offered. For anything else about a vehicle, contact the consultant shown on the listing.']],
 ['t-bidding','6. Registering and bidding',[
  'You must be 18 or over and give your legal name, date of birth, residential address and an Australian mobile. Business buyers can add their company name and ABN for their tax invoice. Only registered bidders can bid.',
  '[[deposit]]Before your first bid you verify your mobile with an SMS code, verify your identity with a driver licence or passport and a selfie, through Stripe Identity, and pay a bidding deposit (section 8). Your name and date of birth must match your ID.',
  '[[transfer]]Before your first bid you verify your mobile with an SMS code and your identity with a driver licence or passport and a selfie, through Stripe Identity. Your name and date of birth must match your ID. That’s all: there’s no deposit and no card.',
  'One account per person. Don’t bid for someone else unless we’ve approved it in writing. Don’t use more than one account, collude with other bidders, or bid to inflate a price. If we close an account because a vehicle wasn’t paid for, the same person can’t open another one (section 11).',
  '<b id="t-live">Live auctions.</b> Every vehicle is offered in a live auction, at a published start time: our auctioneer offers the vehicles one at a time, in the published order, and you bid online as it happens, in the live room (before a vehicle is offered, you can leave an early bid on its listing). There’s no video of the auction: while a vehicle is up, the room shows its photos and the seller’s walkaround video beside the price and the countdown, and the auctioneer’s calls appear on the page. The time shown for a vehicle before its turn is only an estimate. Once a vehicle is offered it has a short countdown, shown on the page, and every bid near the end resets the countdown so other bidders can answer. The hammer falls when the countdown ends, or earlier if the auctioneer calls fair warning and closes bidding.',
  'Bids: each bid is an offer to buy the vehicle at that amount plus the buyer’s premium and fees, and its all-in cost is shown before you place it. On a listing you confirm each bid. Before you bid in the live room, you read the auction’s conditions (the key points of these terms) and accept them once, on entering; we record that you did, and after that each tap of a bid button is a bid. You can withdraw a bid until the hammer falls: an early bid from the listing any time before the vehicle is offered, and a bid in the live room until the countdown ends. The price is then worked out again as if you’d never bid, and the countdown gives the room a moment to answer. Once the hammer falls on your bid, the sale is made and your bid can’t be withdrawn. Bidding and withdrawing over and over to move a price is unfair bidding (below).',
  'Early bids: until a vehicle is offered, you can set the most you’ll pay, and we bid for you, one increment at a time, only as far as needed to keep you in front, up to your maximum. Nobody else sees your maximum. If two bidders set the same maximum, the one who set it first wins, against early and live bids alike.',
  'Reserve: if bidding reaches the seller’s reserve, the vehicle is on the market and sells to the highest bid when the hammer falls. The live room shows when the reserve is met. The seller may lower or remove the reserve until the hammer falls, never raise it once there are bids. If the hammer falls below the reserve, the vehicle is <b>passed in</b>: it isn’t sold, and neither you nor the seller owes anything. If you were the highest bidder, one of our consultants will be in touch about the next auction. We don’t refer bids to the seller or take offers instead of the auction: a vehicle offered in the live auction is sold only under the hammer, or not at all.',
  '<b id="t-after">Nothing is sold after the auction.</b> A truck that’s passed in, or whose buyer doesn’t pay, goes into a later auction unless its owner withdraws it. We don’t sell it by private treaty in between, and nobody at Super Trucker will offer you one that way. If an owner offers to sell you a truck you found through us, that sale still goes through us (section 18).',
  'In a live auction the auctioneer may also take bids by phone or in the room, only from registered members with a verified ID and only on their instruction. Those bids go through the same system as online bids, with the same checks, and are marked as floor bids. The auctioneer may pause bidding (bids wait while it’s paused), add time, change the order of vehicles not yet offered, or withdraw a vehicle. If there’s a dispute about a bid, the auctioneer decides, using the bids recorded in our system, and may reopen bidding on that vehicle before it’s knocked down. The price and countdown on the page are what count; delays in your own connection are your risk.',
  'If an auction finishes before a vehicle is offered, that vehicle is passed in, not sold: its early bids lapse, and we tell the bidders. A vehicle whose listing was corrected in the last 24 hours isn’t offered until 24 hours after the correction.',
  'The seller can’t bid: sellers, their associates and anyone using the seller’s mobile are blocked from bidding on the seller’s vehicle, and we never bid on a seller’s behalf (there are no vendor bids). We monitor bidding and may cancel bids, void sales and close accounts for shill bidding, collusion or unfair bidding.',
  'Our alerts (outbid, up next, results) are sent as fast as we can, but delivery isn’t guaranteed. Keep an eye on auctions you care about.',
  'If there’s a technical fault or an obvious error in a listing, we may pause the auction, or withdraw the vehicle and offer it at a later auction, and we’ll tell affected bidders. If we cancel someone’s bids (for example for shill bidding), the price is worked out again from the remaining bids, as if those bids were never made.',
  'Fleet and business sales: some vehicles are grouped in a sale page. In the live auction they’re offered one after another, each as its own lot, with its own reserve and its own contract.']],
 ['t-fees','7. Buyer’s premium and fees',[
  'There’s no fee to register, watch or bid. Fees apply only to a vehicle you buy.',
  'Buyer’s premium: {{PREMIUM}} of the price{{PREMIUM_MIN_PART}}, plus GST on the premium. The seller has agreed in writing to us charging it. It’s shown on every listing, in the live room for the vehicle that’s up, and in our advertisements for the auction, and it’s part of every all-in price we show.{{ADMIN_FEE_LINE}}',
  'Nothing is added for transport. You collect the vehicle where it’s kept, at your own cost (section 16); you can ask us for a carrier’s quote.',
  'There’s no surcharge or payment fee: we take PayID and bank transfer only, and we don’t take cards.',
  'GST on the vehicle: bids are GST-inclusive. If the seller is GST-registered and selling a business asset (most trucks), the listing says the price includes GST, and your tax invoice shows it so you can claim it if you’re entitled to. Private sellers don’t charge GST, so that price has none.',
  'Storage of {{STORAGE}} per day applies if you don’t collect on time (section 9).',
  'The all-in amount is shown before you confirm any bid.']],
 ['t-payment','8. Payment',[
  '[[deposit]]Bidding deposit: before you bid, you pay a deposit by PayID or bank transfer, quoting your bidder reference (shown in your account), or to the single-use PayID we show you. It stays yours: it’s a security for the bids you make, not a fee. We hold it in our trust account until it’s applied to a vehicle you buy or returned to you, and we don’t pay interest on it.',
  '[[deposit]]How much: the deposit for a vehicle is {{DEPOSIT_RATE}} of the amount you commit to (at least {{DEPOSIT_MIN}}{{DEPOSIT_CAP_PART}}): your maximum bid while you’re the highest bidder.{{DEPOSIT_ANY}} Your deposit must cover all of these at once. If it doesn’t, the bid isn’t accepted, and we show you how much more you need. When you’re outbid or withdraw a bid, that part of your deposit is free again straight away.',
  '[[deposit]]If you win: the deposit for the price (or the whole invoice, if that’s less) is applied to your invoice straight away and counts towards what you pay. Pay the balance by PayID or bank transfer within {{PAY_DAYS}} business days, quoting your invoice number. If the deposit covers the whole invoice, there’s nothing more to pay.',
  '[[deposit]]The deposit applied to a vehicle is kept only if the sale is cancelled because you didn’t pay (section 11). If the sale is cancelled for any other reason, for example an upheld claim, a title problem, damage before handover or our mistake, it’s returned to your deposit in full, and you can withdraw it.',
  '[[deposit]]Withdrawing: you can ask for any part of your deposit that isn’t holding a bid back at any time from your account, unless you have a vehicle that isn’t paid for yet. We send it to the account it came from, usually the same or next business day. Once your deposit is below the minimum, you can’t bid until you add to it.',
  '[[transfer]]If you win: there’s nothing to pay before you bid, and no deposit. We email your tax invoice when the hammer falls. Pay the full amount by PayID or bank transfer within {{PAY_DAYS}} business days, quoting your invoice number.',
  '[[transfer]]Buying with finance: get pre-approved before you bid, because a bid the hammer falls on is binding. Your lender can pay us directly: tell us who they are when you win, and their payment counts as yours. If your lender needs a little longer, ask us before the due date.',
  'How to pay: by PayID or bank transfer to the account shown in your account and on your invoice page, or to the single-use PayID we show you for that payment. Where your invoice shows our BPAY biller code, you can also pay by BPAY from your bank, using your own Customer Reference Number (CRN): it’s the same for every payment you make to us. BPAY can take a business day or two to reach us, so allow for it before the due date. We don’t accept cards, cash or cheques. A truck is a large payment: check your bank’s daily transfer limit before the auction and raise it, or arrange a same-day transfer with your branch. A payment is on time if you send it by the due date and it clears in the normal course. We send the address and your release code only once the money has cleared into our account.',
  'Where your money goes: what you pay for a vehicle is paid into our trust account and held there for the seller, as the motor dealer and agent trust account laws require, until the sale completes. Then we pay the seller (or their lender) from it and take our fees.',
  'Pay from an account in your own name, or your business’s name if you’re buying for it (a joint account you’re named on is fine), or have your lender pay us. Money from anyone else’s account isn’t a payment by you: we return it to the account it came from. It protects you and the seller from fraud.',
  'Pay Super Trucker only, never the seller. Money paid to the seller or to any account other than the one shown in your account or on your invoice page isn’t a payment to us, unless the wrong details came from us. We will never change our bank details by email, SMS or phone. If anyone asks you to, don’t pay: call us on {{PHONE}}.',
  'Interest: if your balance is overdue, we may charge interest on the overdue amount at {{LATE_INTEREST}} a year, worked out daily from the due date until it’s paid. We don’t charge any other late-payment fee.',
  'Refunds go back to the account you paid from. If you owe us something under these terms (for example storage), we may take it out of a refund (or your deposit, if you have one) before we pay it, and we’ll show you how it was worked out.',
  'Buying for a business: the business name and ABN in your account go on your tax invoices, as they were when you won; you’re responsible for them being right. Approved dealer accounts can pay several invoices with one transfer quoting their own payment reference; each invoice keeps its own due date.',
  'You receive a tax invoice by email when you win, and a receipt when you’ve paid in full. Your paperwork includes our notice that the vehicle was sold by auction as agent for its owner, the statutory warranty statement and the PPSR search details.']],
 ['t-title','9. Title, risk and collection',[
  'Title: we search the PPSR before listing. Any registered finance is paid out of the sale price before the seller is paid, so you receive the vehicle free of registered security interests once you’ve paid in full. If a title problem appears that we can’t fix, we’ll cancel the sale and refund everything you paid.',
  'Ownership (title) passes to you when we receive full payment in cleared funds. The registration transfer that follows puts the registration into your name.',
  'Risk passes to you at the handover, or at the end of your collection window if you haven’t collected, whichever comes first. Until then the vehicle is in the seller’s hands and at the seller’s risk: the seller must look after it with reasonable care, keep it insured and in the same condition, and not work it. We never have the vehicle. Your protection is that we hold your money in trust until the handover is done and your claim window has closed: if the vehicle is damaged, stolen or materially changed before the handover, you may cancel for a full refund (or go ahead, at a price you and the seller agree through us). Arrange your own insurance from the handover, or from the day the registration is in your name if that’s earlier.',
  'Collection: once you’ve paid in full and we’ve lodged the seller’s notice of disposal (or there was nothing to lodge, because it’s sold unregistered), book a time from your invoice. We agree it with the seller and send you the address and a 6-digit release code. You don’t have to have put the registration into your own name first, and we don’t ask you for proof of it. Collect within {{COLLECT_DAYS}} business days of the day we tell you it’s ready (we can agree more time for interstate buyers and transport companies if you ask before the window ends).',
  'The handover: check the vehicle against the listing before you give the release code. The seller enters your code on our handover page, with the odometer reading and the keys handed over. The code is your sign-off that you’ve taken the vehicle, and it starts the claim window in section 12. If something is materially different from the listing (new damage, a missing key, parts removed, it no longer starts), don’t give the code: call us from the yard. You choose: go ahead, or cancel the sale for a full refund.',
  'Tolls, fines and charges from before the handover are the seller’s. If one is sent to you, tell us and we’ll deal with it.',
  'If the seller doesn’t hand the vehicle over, or the sale is cancelled after the registration transfer because of the seller or us, we’ll cancel the sale, refund everything you paid and arrange for the registration to go back to the seller. You can also recover the transfer fee and stamp duty you paid (where your state doesn’t refund them) and reasonable costs you can’t get back, such as a booked carrier, from whoever caused it.',
  'Registration transfer: after you pay in full, we lodge the seller’s notice of disposal with their state’s authority as their agent, using the details we already hold, and the seller supplies any inspection certificate the state needs (section 10). Putting the registration into your own name is then your step: you pay the transfer fee and duty and complete it with your state’s transport authority within the time your state requires. We fill the form in for you from your verified account details, and your invoice has the button. You don’t have to send us proof, and it is not a condition of collecting. If you can’t or don’t want to register it in that state, you can take it unregistered: the registration is cancelled and the plates come off at the handover. Unregistered vehicles: you confirm the certificate of sale in your name, which is your record of ownership, and how you’ll move the vehicle (a carrier, your own float or trailer, or a permit).',
  'Unregistered vehicles: one with no plates leaves on a carrier, a float or a trailer, or is driven under a current unregistered vehicle permit whose number the seller records on the handover page before the keys change hands. That is not anyone being difficult: letting an unregistered vehicle be driven on a road is an offence by whoever permits it as well as whoever drives it, so without one of those the handover can’t be completed. A written-off vehicle can’t be driven away at all.',
  'Whoever collects must be named on your booking and show photo ID matching that name. A transport company must quote your booking reference. The seller hands over the vehicle only when the release code works. You’re responsible for anyone you send to collect (a driver or a transport company) as if they were you. Never pay the seller anything, and don’t agree extras or side deals at the handover: what’s sold is what’s in the listing.',
  'The keys, books and accessories listed are handed over with the vehicle. Anything else the seller leaves in it isn’t part of the sale.',
  'The odometer reading, the keys handed over and anything noted at the handover are recorded.',
  'Storage: if you don’t collect within the window, storage of {{STORAGE}} per day applies from the next day and must be paid before release. It covers the vehicle being kept for you. There’s no storage for any day the delay was caused by us or the seller, and none before the seller’s notice of disposal is lodged and we’ve told you it’s ready.',
  'Abandonment: if you still haven’t collected {{ABANDON_DAYS}} business days after we give you written notice, the vehicle may be dealt with as uncollected goods under the law of the state it’s in (the Disposal of Uncollected Goods Act 1967 in Queensland, the Uncollected Goods Act 1995 in New South Wales or the Disposal of Uncollected Goods Act 1970 in Western Australia), after the notices that law requires, and you’re paid what’s left after storage, the reasonable costs of selling it and anything else you owe under these terms.']],
 ['t-states','10. Registration, transfer and inspection certificates (rules differ by state)',[
  'Every listing says whether the vehicle is registered (with its plate, state and expiry) or unregistered (sold without plates).',
  'You pay transfer fees, stamp duty, registration and plate fees, and any late-transfer penalties, and you must transfer the registration within the time the state requires (usually 14 days). Those are charged by the state to you, in your own name, so they are the one part of this we cannot do for you. We lodge the seller’s part (a notice of disposal, or starting the transfer online) for them once the sale is paid. Your invoice has the button and the right authority for the vehicle’s state; we remind you if the deadline is getting close.',
  'Unregistered vehicles can’t be driven on the road by anyone, including you. Move it by carrier, float or trailer, or under a permit you get from the state’s transport authority before collection day. The permits differ: Queensland’s unregistered vehicle permit covers a set trip for 1 to 7 days; New South Wales issues one at a service centre, not online; Western Australia’s temporary movement permit lasts 48 hours, is arranged by phone for a heavy vehicle, and is for a trip to a repairer, an inspection station or to be licensed, not simply to drive it home. Check with the state before you bid. An unregistered vehicle also has no compulsory third party insurance beyond what a permit includes. To register it, apply to your state’s transport authority with the certificate of sale and any inspection it requires: that is a new registration, not a transfer, so expect a full inspection first.',
  'Inspection certificates. <b>Queensland</b>: a registered truck over 4.5 tonnes GVM is transferred on a current certificate of inspection, and a lighter one on a safety certificate. <b>New South Wales</b>: nothing more is needed to transfer a current registration, but the law doesn’t let a vehicle be auctioned with its plates on unless a current inspection report (issued in the 42 days before) is shown with it, so a registered truck in New South Wales has its report in the listing’s photos, or the listing says its registration was first issued or renewed in the 90 days before the auction. Otherwise it’s sold without plates, and the listing says why it has none. <b>Western Australia</b>: nothing more is needed to transfer a current licence (registration). Where a certificate is needed the seller supplies it: the listing shows its date (or why the vehicle is exempt) before bidding opens. If it lapses before the transfer, the seller gets a new one at their cost; if the vehicle then needs repairs to pass and the seller doesn’t have them done before the handover, you can cancel the sale for a full refund.',
  'Interstate buyers: registration usually transfers only to someone who can register it in that state. If you can’t, choose to take it unregistered: the seller cancels the registration and keeps the plates, and you register it in your state, which may need an inspection.',
  'Driving it away: whoever drives it needs the licence class for it (LR, MR, HR, HC or MC), and it must be driven within its registration and the heavy vehicle rules (mass, dimensions, any permit). That’s yours to arrange. The GVM is on every listing.',
  'Remaining registration isn’t refunded or adjusted between buyer and seller. The listing shows any defect notice or registration condition the seller has told us about.',
  'Written-off vehicles: if a vehicle is on a written-off vehicle register, the listing says so. Statutory write-offs can never be re-registered. Check whether a repairable write-off can be registered in your state before you bid.']],
 ['t-default','11. If a buyer doesn’t pay or collect',[
  'If you don’t pay on time, we’ll remind you by SMS and email. If you still haven’t paid 1 business day after that reminder, we may cancel the sale, offer the vehicle at a later auction, and suspend your account.',
  'Closing your account: if we cancel a sale because you didn’t pay, we close your account for bidding. Your bids on other vehicles are cancelled, and you can’t open a new account: we keep a one-way code made from your name and date of birth, mobile and email (it can’t be turned back into your details) to check new accounts against. If you think we’ve made a mistake, contact us (section 15) and we’ll review it.',
  '[[deposit]]If we cancel because you didn’t pay, we keep the deposit that was applied to that vehicle (it’s shown on your invoice), and half of it goes to the seller. There’s no separate cancellation fee: it’s the deposit or nothing, never both. The rest of your deposit stays yours. Our payment reminder tells you this before we cancel. The deposit is our and the seller’s genuine estimate of the costs of a failed sale (offering it again, the seller’s lost time and the vehicle being off the market), and it’s capped so it stays in proportion to them.',
  '[[deposit]]If the vehicle then sells for less, you may also have to pay the difference and the reasonable costs of selling it again, less the deposit we kept. We’ll give you a statement showing how it’s worked out, and we won’t claim more than our and the seller’s actual loss.',
  '[[transfer]]There’s no cancellation fee. If the vehicle then sells for less, you may have to pay the difference and the reasonable costs of selling it again. We’ll give you a statement showing how it’s worked out, and we won’t claim more than our and the seller’s actual loss.',
  'Anything you owe under these terms is a debt. If it stays unpaid, we may refer it to a debt collector or take legal action, and recover our reasonable costs of doing so, within what the law allows.',
  'Not collecting on time: storage and abandonment are covered in section 9.']],
 ['t-claims','12. If the vehicle isn’t as described (claims)',[
  'You can make a claim if the vehicle is <b>materially different</b> from its listing, for example: a different make, model, build year or VIN; manual listed as automatic (or the reverse); a different fuel type; an undisclosed written-off or stolen status; undisclosed finance; an odometer materially different from the listing; a key feature listed that isn’t there; or major damage the listing didn’t show or mention.',
  'Claims don’t cover general wear, mechanical faults that weren’t described and couldn’t be seen in the seller’s photos or video, or anything disclosed in the listing or the seller’s declarations. The listing is what counts: something an owner said at a viewing that isn’t in the listing isn’t something we checked (section 5), though your rights against anyone who misled you aren’t affected.',
  'How: lodge the claim from your invoice, with photos, before you accept handover, or within {{CLAIM_DAYS}} business days after handover. For a wrong VIN or build year, an undisclosed written-off or stolen status, undisclosed finance or odometer tampering, which can take longer to find, contact us within 30 days of handover. Don’t modify, repair or use the vehicle (beyond getting it home) while we review it. Completing the registration transfer is fine. This window is for our claims process; it doesn’t take away any right you have under the Australian Consumer Law.',
  'We compare the vehicle with the listing as it was at the moment of sale (we keep a copy), give the seller the chance to respond, and give you a decision in writing within 2 business days of receiving what we need. If your claim is upheld, you can cancel the sale for a full refund of everything you paid, or agree a price adjustment. The seller’s payout is held while a claim is open.',
  'If you cancel after collecting, return the vehicle to where you collected it in the condition you received it, or let us arrange its return; we’ll agree reasonable return costs with you as part of the claim. Disputes with the seller about the vehicle go through this process first, so we can help resolve them.',
  'Damage before the handover is covered by section 9: don’t give the release code, and call us.']],
 ['t-liability','13. Our liability',[
  'Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or changes any right or remedy you have under the Australian Consumer Law, or any other law, that can’t lawfully be excluded.',
  'Subject to that: we’re responsible for loss caused by our own negligence, fraud or breach of these terms. We aren’t responsible for a vehicle’s condition beyond what section 4, section 9, section 12 and the law provide; for what the seller tells us or you, beyond the checks we say we make (section 3); for a seller’s premises or what happens there, which the seller controls and we don’t attend (sections 5 and 16); for the independent mechanics, lenders, insurers, carriers and other partners you choose to use (their own terms apply); or for events outside our reasonable control (section 17).',
  'Neither we nor the seller is responsible for indirect loss that wasn’t reasonably foreseeable when the sale was made, such as lost profits or lost business.',
  'Where the law lets us limit our liability for a service we supply, it’s limited to supplying the service again or paying the cost of having it supplied again. This doesn’t limit your rights under section 12 or under the Australian Consumer Law.']],
 ['t-privacy','14. Privacy',[
  'We collect your details to run auctions, verify identity, process sales and prevent fraud. The listing doesn’t name the owner or give their street address. We give the address where a vehicle is kept only to a verified member with a viewing we’ve booked and to the buyer with a confirmed collection, and we tell the owner the name of whoever is coming, so they know who to expect. For the registration transfer, the owner’s part gets only what the state’s form asks for about you (for example your licence or customer number in New South Wales and Queensland), and nothing more. See our <a class="blue" href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a>.']],
 ['t-complaints','15. Complaints and disputes',[
  'Contact us first on {{PHONE}} or {{EMAIL}}. We acknowledge complaints within 1 business day and aim to resolve them within 10 business days.',
  'If you’re not happy with our answer, ask for a review by a manager who wasn’t involved. We’ll give you our final answer in writing, with our reasons.',
  'If that doesn’t resolve it, you can contact the fair trading or consumer affairs agency in your state or territory, or apply to your state’s civil and administrative tribunal or small claims court. If we both agree, we can also use an independent mediator, with the cost shared equally.']],
 ['t-site','16. Collecting it from where it’s kept',[
  'You, and anyone collecting for you, go only at the confirmed time, follow the site’s safety directions, and stay with your host. It’s the owner’s workplace or property, not ours.',
  'Bring what the vehicle needs to be moved safely and legally: a driver licensed for its class, or a carrier or float with the right equipment. It’s handed over as it stands: it may be low on fuel, and one that’s been parked may need its batteries charged. The seller doesn’t have to load it, drive it for you or lend you equipment.',
  'Anything that needs a float, a crane or lifting gear must be moved by a person or business qualified to do it, with their own insurance. Tell us when you book, and we’ll agree the arrangements with the seller.',
  'Don’t repair it, remove parts or road test it at the seller’s place, and don’t drive an unregistered vehicle on a road unless you have a permit.',
  'You’re responsible for damage or injury that you or your collector cause at the seller’s place, except to the extent the seller or we caused it.',
  'If collection can’t go ahead safely, stop and call us. We’ll arrange another time, and your collection window is extended.',
  'Delivery: if you’d rather not collect, ask for a quote from a carrier. The carrier you book collects for you with your release code, and is responsible for the vehicle from the handover.',
  'Before you put it to work: make sure it meets work health and safety laws and anything your state requires for the work it will do (for example a crane, a tailgate loader or a dangerous goods tanker). Older trucks can contain hazardous materials (asbestos in brakes or gaskets), fluids, gas cylinders or batteries: handle them lawfully. Heavy or oversize vehicles must be moved under the Heavy Vehicle National Law in Queensland and New South Wales, and Western Australia’s own heavy vehicle rules, with any permit needed. Anyone you send should carry suitable public liability insurance.']],
 ['t-errors','17. Errors, outages and events outside our control',[
  'If the live auction is disrupted (our website or app, or a widespread outage), the auctioneer pauses bidding and then resumes it, reopens the vehicle that was up, or passes it in to a later auction, and we tell the bidders. We’re not responsible for bids that don’t reach us because of your own device, internet connection or settings, so leave an early bid on vehicles that matter to you.',
  'If a listing or an invoice has an obvious mistake that you would reasonably have noticed (for example an estimate missing a zero, or another vehicle’s photos), we may cancel the affected bids or sale and refund everything you paid. We’ll tell you why.',
  'Our system records the time and amount of every bid. If there’s a disagreement about bids, we use those records, and we’ll show you the relevant part if you ask.',
  'Neither we nor the seller is responsible for a delay or failure caused by something outside reasonable control, such as a natural disaster, flood, fire, a public health order, a widespread failure of internet, banking or payment systems, or government action. We’ll tell you as soon as we can, and deadlines for paying, transferring and collecting are extended while it lasts. If it lasts more than 20 business days, you or the seller may cancel the sale, and you get a full refund.']],
 ['t-responsible','18. Your responsibilities',[
  'Give us true information, keep your login private, and tell us straight away if you think someone else has used your account. You’re responsible for bids made from your account, unless they were made after you told us it had been compromised, or because of a failure in our security.',
  'If you buy for a company or business, you confirm you’re authorised to bind it, and it’s responsible for paying. If you weren’t authorised, you’re responsible as if you’d bought the vehicle yourself.',
  'Don’t interfere with an auction: no shill bidding, no colluding with other bidders, and no bidding and withdrawing to move a price.',
  '<b>Every sale goes through us.</b> Don’t contact, visit or approach an owner about a vehicle listed with us except at a viewing or collection we’ve booked. Don’t make an owner an offer, ask them to deal direct or agree a side deal, before, during or after the auction; if an owner suggests it, say no and tell us. Keep the address to yourself. If you buy a vehicle we introduced you to from its owner other than through us, while it’s listed or within {{EXCLUSIVITY_DAYS}} days after, you owe us the buyer’s premium on the price you paid (section 5). Going around us is also a serious breach: we may cancel your bids and sales and close your account.',
  'You’ll pay us back for loss we reasonably suffer because you broke these terms or acted fraudulently, or because of something you, your mechanic or your collector did at a viewing, at the handover or to the seller, including amounts we have to pay the seller or others. This doesn’t apply to the extent the loss was caused by us, the seller or anyone acting for us.']],
 ['t-notices','19. Notices',[
  'We send notices about your bids, purchases and account by email, SMS, app notification or on your account page, using the details on your account, so please keep them up to date. An email or SMS notice counts as received when we send it, unless we learn that it didn’t arrive.',
  'You can send us a notice by email to {{EMAIL}} or through Contact us. Notices about a purchase should quote your invoice number.']],
 ['t-general','20. General',[
  'These terms are governed by the laws of Queensland, Australia, where our auctions are run from. Nothing here stops you from using a tribunal or court in your own state where the law allows, or takes away a protection the law of your state gives you.',
  'We may update these terms, and we’ll tell you before we do. A change never applies to a sale already made: the version you accepted when you placed a bid applies to that sale, and we’ll ask you to accept any new version before your next bid. If you don’t want to accept it, you can close your account.',
  'For each purchase, these terms, the listing as it was when the sale was made, and your invoice are the whole agreement. Our <a class="blue" href="/website-terms">Website terms</a> cover using the website and app.',
  'If part of these terms can’t be enforced, it’s read down or left out and the rest still applies. If we don’t enforce a right straight away, we haven’t given it up.',
  '“Business day” means a weekday that isn’t a public holiday in Queensland or a national public holiday. Times are Brisbane time unless we say otherwise.',
  'We may transfer our rights and obligations to a business that takes over our auctions. We’ll tell you if we do, and it won’t reduce your rights.',
  'This version: 15 November 2026.']]
];

export const SELLER_AGREEMENT_VERSION_LABEL = "Version 15 November 2026";
export const SELLER_AGREEMENT: [string, string, string[]][] = [
 ['s-parties','1. This agreement',[
  'This Seller Agency Agreement is between you (the “seller”) and {{LEGAL_NAME}} (ABN {{ABN}}) (“Super Trucker”), licensed as {{LICENCES}}. It applies to the vehicle described in your sell form or named in your listing link. You sign it electronically (by drawing your signature, or typing your full name if you can’t draw one), and we record the date, time and device. When you use the sell form, you confirm it again with your verified identity before the vehicle goes live. We email you a copy of exactly what you signed.',
  'It’s your written authority for us to sell the vehicle (the consignment agreement the motor dealer laws require). Together with your sell form and your answers, it records who you are and where the vehicle is kept, our licence details, the vehicle, any finance owing on it, your reserve, how we pay you and how long the authority lasts. Your authority lasts 90 days from when you sign, unless we both agree in writing to extend it.',
  'You appoint Super Trucker as your exclusive agent to sell the vehicle in a live online auction, conducted by a licensed auctioneer, and sold under the hammer. If bidding doesn’t reach your reserve, it’s passed in and stays yours, and it goes into our next auction unless you say no (section 12). We don’t sell trucks after the auction by private treaty. We never give a statutory warranty, so we don’t list a vehicle that would carry one: tell us if you’re a motor dealer, or if you bought this vehicle to resell it, because a trade owner’s vehicle can carry one (in Western Australia, even at auction).',
  'We’re never at your vehicle. You send us the photos and a walkaround video (section 7), and we check them against your papers, the registration record and a PPSR search. The vehicle stays with you from listing to handover: buyers view it at your place by appointment, and the buyer collects it from you once they’ve paid us in full (section 7). There’s no tow and no depot.',
  'We sell as your agent. The listing doesn’t name you, and it shows your suburb, not your street. We give your address only to a verified member whose viewing we’ve agreed with you, and to the buyer once we’ve agreed their collection time with you, and we tell you who is coming first. Every buyer question, problem and claim comes to us, and we deal with you.']],
 ['s-exclusive','2. Exclusive authority, and buyers we introduce',[
  '<b>Exclusive.</b> For the 90 days of your authority (section 1), only we sell the vehicle. If it’s sold in any other way while your authority lasts, by you or anyone else, to anyone, you pay us the buyer’s premium we would have earned on the sale price: {{PREMIUM}} of it, plus GST{{SELLER_FEE_ALSO}}. If you withdraw it first (section 8) and then sell it to someone we didn’t introduce, you pay only the withdrawal fee.',
  '<b>Buyers we introduce.</b> Buyers come to your place to view the vehicle and to collect it, so this is how we’re paid for bringing them. For {{EXCLUSIVITY_DAYS}} days after your authority ends, or after you withdraw the vehicle, the same amount is payable if you sell it to someone we introduced: anyone we named to you in writing (every viewing and collection we book names the visitor), anyone who bid on it with us, and anyone who tells you, or who you know, found it through Super Trucker.',
  'If anyone asks to buy it direct, at a viewing or at any other time, say no and tell us the same day. Each visitor has agreed in writing not to ask, and to pay us the same premium if they buy it around us; a sale outside Super Trucker also has no trust account, title check or claims process behind it for either of you.',
  'The amount is what we lose when a sale we advertised, checked and set up goes around us, and no more. You pay it once, on the price the vehicle sold for (if you don’t tell us the price, on the low end of our estimate), within 7 days of our invoice. We don’t also collect it from the buyer.']],
 ['s-fees','3. Fees',[
  'Seller fee: {{SELLER_FEE}}. It’s earned only when the vehicle sells, and it’s taken from the sale proceeds.',
  'Inspection before listing (optional): if you ask for it in this agreement, we have a mechanic inspect the vehicle before it lists and show the report to buyers. The fee ({{PRE_INSPECTION_FEE}} including GST, as shown when you sign) is taken from the sale proceeds when it sells; if it doesn’t sell, there’s nothing to pay. The report describes the vehicle as the mechanic found it; it doesn’t change what you’ve declared.',
  'There’s no charge for the appraisal, checking your photos and video, our report, the PPSR search, arranging viewings or arranging the handover, unless we agree otherwise in writing.',
  'Buyer’s premium: by signing, you agree in writing to us charging the buyer a buyer’s premium of {{PREMIUM}} of the price{{PREMIUM_MIN_PART}}, plus GST{{ADMIN_FEE_PART}}, and to bidders being told about it on every listing, in our advertisements and in the live room, as the law requires. It’s ours and doesn’t reduce your proceeds.']],
 ['s-reserve','4. The estimate, your reserve and your instructions',[
  'Before the auction we agree an auction estimate with you: our opinion of where bidding is likely to end, from recent sales of similar vehicles and your photos, video and answers. It’s shown on the listing. It isn’t a valuation or a promise of a price.',
  'You set the reserve when you sign. It stays secret from bidders, and it can’t be above the estimate’s low end: if you want a higher reserve, we’ll look at whether the evidence supports a higher estimate, and if it doesn’t, the reserve stays at or below the low end. We record your reserve, as auction law requires.',
  'You may lower or remove the reserve at any time until the hammer falls: from your seller dashboard, or by phoning us during the auction, when the auctioneer records your instruction for you. You can’t raise it once bidding has started. Each change is recorded as your instruction, with the time.',
  'You authorise us to sell to the highest bid at or above the reserve when the hammer falls. If there’s no reserve, the vehicle sells to the highest bid. If bidding doesn’t reach the reserve, the vehicle is passed in: it isn’t sold and nothing is payable. We offer it again at our next live auction unless you tell us not to (section 12).']],
 ['s-nobid','5. No seller bidding',[
  'You, your family, employees and associates must not bid on the vehicle or ask anyone to bid for you, and we never bid on your behalf. If that happens, we may void the sale and cancel the listing, and our seller fee plus the buyer’s premium is payable on the higher of the highest bid and your reserve, plus our reasonable costs.']],
 ['s-warranties','6. What you promise us (and buyers rely on)',[
  'You are the owner of the vehicle, or you are authorised in writing by every owner (or by the company or trust that owns it) to sell it.',
  'The vehicle is free of security interests and charges, except finance you’ve told us about. You authorise us to pay that finance out from the sale proceeds and to deal with your lender to do so.',
  'The vehicle isn’t stolen, and isn’t written off unless you’ve told us. The VIN and engine number are genuine and haven’t been altered.',
  'You don’t know of any tampering with the odometer, other than anything you’ve told us.',
  'There’s no defect notice, registration condition or unpaid toll or fine on the vehicle that you haven’t told us about.',
  'Your answers to our questions (accidents, flood or hail damage, modifications, warning lights, whether it starts and drives, known faults, keys and service books) are true and complete as far as you know, and you’ve told us about every fault you know of.',
  'You’ve told us whether you’re selling as a private person or in the course of a business. You’re not a motor dealer, and you didn’t buy this vehicle to resell it, unless you’ve told us: the dealer laws treat a trade owner’s vehicle differently, and in Western Australia we can’t auction one on these terms.',
  'You’ve told us about any use as a hire, rental, mining, waste, dangerous goods or livestock vehicle, any safety recall you know hasn’t been fixed, any engine, gearbox or diff rebuild or replacement, any emissions system fault, delete or tune, and any modification that wouldn’t pass an inspection or isn’t on the vehicle’s modification plate. These answers are shown on the listing.',
  'The photos and video you send are of this vehicle, taken by you for this listing in the last 14 days, and show it as it is: no filters, edits or old photos, and every damage you know of shown. We’re never at the vehicle, so we and the buyers rely on them, and on your answers, as accurate. They’re yours to give. Film and photograph only the vehicle: keep street numbers, street signs, mail, people and other vehicles’ plates out of shot. If your business name or phone number is painted on it, tell us. We check, and we remove the location your phone records.',
  'If the vehicle is registered, you give us what its state needs before the auction, from an approved inspection station, and keep it current until the handover, at your cost. In Queensland: a certificate of inspection for a vehicle over 4.5 tonnes GVM, or a safety certificate for a lighter one. In New South Wales: a current inspection report, issued in the 42 days before the auction, unless the registration was first issued or renewed in the 90 days before it; the law doesn’t let a vehicle be auctioned with its plates on without one, so otherwise you hand the plates in and it’s sold unregistered. In Western Australia: nothing more. If it lapses, you get a new one; if the vehicle then needs repairs to pass, you have them done at your cost before the handover, or the buyer may cancel and section 13 applies.',
  'Tolls, fines and registration charges up to the handover are yours.',
  'You must tell us straight away if anything you’ve told us stops being true.']],
 ['s-obligations','7. Photos, video, viewings and the handover',[
  'Photos and video: send us the photos with the sell form, and the walkaround video through your seller dashboard. We tell you exactly what to film: starting it from cold, the dash with the engine running, a slow walk around it and the inside, and moving it under its own power if it’s safe and legal where you are. We can’t list it without them, and we may ask for more if something isn’t clear. We check them before they go on the listing.',
  'Keep the vehicle at the address you gave us, insured, and in the same condition as in your photos and video, until the buyer collects it. A listed vehicle is parked, not worked: move it only as needed to keep it in condition, and tell us if the odometer goes up by more than 50 km, or anything else changes, so we can correct the listing. Don’t use it at all once it’s sold. Keep the batteries charged and some fuel in the tank.',
  '<b>Viewings.</b> Buyers can view the vehicle at your address, by appointment. We agree each time with you first, then tell you in writing who is coming; nobody we haven’t named to you has a booking, so turn them away and tell us. Check the visitor’s photo ID against the name we gave you. Show them the vehicle, start it and let them hear it run. No road test, and nothing is taken apart. You’re the occupier: keep the area safe, tell visitors your site rules, and stay with them. Answer their questions truthfully, but don’t discuss price or a private sale (section 2), and if you tell a visitor something that isn’t in the listing, tell us too, so every bidder has it. If you can’t host viewings at all, tell us before it’s listed and the listing will say so.',
  'Mechanical inspections: a visitor may bring a mechanic to a viewing. If a bidder who can’t get there orders an inspection through us, give our partner mechanic access at a time we agree with you (we call first). The mechanic may start and run the vehicle and look underneath where they safely can.',
  '<b>The handover.</b> Once the buyer has paid us in full, they book a time to collect it and we agree it with you. We send you a handover link and tell you who is collecting. When they arrive: check their photo ID against the name we gave you, let them check the vehicle against the listing, then open the link and enter the 6-digit release code they give you, the odometer reading and the keys handed over. If the code doesn’t work, don’t hand it over: call us. Have every key, book and accessory in the listing ready. You don’t have to load the vehicle or lend equipment. Never accept money from anyone for it: the buyer has paid us, and we pay you.',
  'Sold without plates: an unregistered vehicle leaves your place on a carrier, a float or a trailer, or under a permit whose number you enter on the handover page. Letting an unregistered vehicle be driven onto a road is an offence by whoever permits it, so the handover page won’t complete without one of those. That protects you.',
  'If the vehicle isn’t ready at the agreed time without good reason, you pay the buyer’s reasonable wasted costs (for example a carrier’s call-out). We’ll show you how it’s worked out first, and you won’t pay it if the reason was outside your control.',
  'The vehicle stays at your risk, and insured by you, until the handover is recorded. If it’s damaged, stolen or changes materially before then, tell us immediately. The buyer may then cancel.',
  'Before the handover, remove your toll tag, fuel cards and belongings, any telematics or tracking unit that isn’t in the listing, and sign out of the vehicle’s apps and paired phones. Anything left in it isn’t part of the sale.',
  'Transfer: you authorise us to lodge your part of the registration transfer (a notice of disposal, or starting the transfer online) for you, as your agent under this authority, using the details you have given us. We do it once the buyer has paid in full and within the time your state requires, and we text you when it is done: there is nothing for you to lodge and nothing for you to chase. You still supply any certificate your state needs (section 6). If the buyer takes the vehicle unregistered, we cancel the registration for you; take the plates off at the handover and return them to the transport authority. Putting the vehicle into the buyer’s own name is the buyer’s step and nothing about it comes back to you.']],
 ['s-withdraw','8. Withdrawing the vehicle',[
  'You can withdraw the vehicle free of charge before it’s listed.',
  'After it’s listed, you can withdraw it by telling us, until bidding reaches the reserve. A withdrawal fee of {{WITHDRAWAL_FEE}} applies to cover the costs of checking your photos and video, our report, the PPSR search and marketing. There’s no fee if you withdraw because of something outside your control (for example the vehicle is stolen or damaged through no fault of yours). Once bidding has reached the reserve, the vehicle can’t be withdrawn. Section 2 still applies to a sale to someone we introduced.']],
 ['s-default','9. If the buyer doesn’t pay',[
  'The vehicle is handed over only once the buyer has paid us in full, so it stays with you if the buyer doesn’t pay. We then offer it at a later auction, without a new seller fee.',
  'If we keep a deposit or charge a cancellation fee to a buyer who didn’t pay, we pay you half of it. You authorise us to deal with the buyer first. If we decide not to pursue the buyer, or haven’t recovered what they owe within 30 days, you may pursue them yourself, and we’ll give you the records you need.']],
 ['s-settlement','10. Getting paid',[
  'The buyer pays Super Trucker. We pay you the sale price less our seller fee (plus GST on it), any finance we pay out to your lender, and any other costs you’ve agreed to in writing.',
  'We pay you within {{PAYOUT_DAYS}} business days after both (a) the handover is recorded with the buyer’s release code, and (b) the buyer’s claim window ({{CLAIM_DAYS}} business days after handover) has closed with no open claim. You get a settlement statement.',
  'We pay only into the bank account you gave us when you signed, which we confirm with you by phone. We’ll never ask you to change it by email.',
  'If the finance owing is more than the sale price, you must pay your lender the difference before we can complete the sale.',
  'Sale money is held in our trust account for you, as the motor dealer and agent trust account laws require (for example Queensland’s Agents Financial Administration Act 2014 and the consignment rules in New South Wales and Western Australia), from when the buyer pays until it’s paid out under this section.']],
 ['s-claims','11. Buyer claims and clawback',[
  'If a buyer claims the vehicle is materially different from the listing (see the Terms of Sale, section 12), we hold your payout while we review it, using the listing as it was at the moment of sale, your photos and video, and your written answers. We send you the claim and the evidence and give you 2 business days to respond before we decide. You can dispute our decision through our complaints process or a tribunal.',
  'If the claim is upheld because of something you told us, sent us or didn’t tell us, as opposed to our own checks, you agree that the sale may be cancelled and the buyer refunded, that you’ll take the vehicle back (and the registration, if it was transferred), and that you’ll repay any money already paid to you, the buyer’s transfer and transport costs they can’t recover, and our reasonable costs. You’ll pay us back for claims, losses and costs caused by a breach of your promises in section 6, or by something you told a visitor that wasn’t true, except to the extent we caused them.',
  'Damage before the handover is yours (section 7). You never need to deal with the buyer about a claim; we do.']],
 ['s-unsold','12. If it doesn’t sell',[
  'Nothing is payable if the vehicle is passed in or otherwise doesn’t sell, unless you withdrew it (section 8) or sold it outside Super Trucker during the exclusive period (section 2).',
  '<b>No sale after the auction.</b> We don’t sell trucks by private treaty after an auction. Under the hammer, a buyer has no acceptable-quality guarantee against you; in a private sale of a goods vehicle they can have, at any price. To sell it on the day, lower your reserve before the hammer falls (section 4): our auctioneer can take your instruction by phone while it’s up.',
  'If it isn’t sold, we offer it again at our next live auction for your state, while your authority lasts (section 1), without a new seller fee. Before it’s listed again we run a fresh PPSR search and listing check, set a fresh estimate with you, and check anything your state needs by the new auction’s date (for example, a New South Wales inspection report must be no more than 42 days old at the auction, and a Queensland certificate must still be current). Your consultant calls you first to agree the reserve: you can lower it. If the next auction is after your authority ends, you sign this agreement again for it.',
  'If you don’t want it offered again, tell us before it’s listed, from your seller dashboard or by calling us. There’s no fee, and the vehicle stays yours. Once it’s listed again, taking it out is a withdrawal (section 8).',
  'You keep ownership of your photos and videos, and you let us use them to market and sell the vehicle and to show the result. The listing text and condition report we write are ours. We may keep showing the listing as a past result.']],
 ['s-cantcomplete','13. If you can’t complete a sale',[
  'If, after the vehicle has sold, you don’t hand it over, it turns out materially different from what you told us or showed us, you can’t supply a certificate your state needs (section 6), or you sell it to someone else, we may cancel the sale and refund the buyer. You’ll then pay our seller fee (if any), the buyer’s premium we lose, the buyer’s costs they can’t recover (for example a carrier’s call-out and transfer costs), and our reasonable costs.',
  'This doesn’t apply if it happened because of something outside your control, for example the vehicle was stolen or destroyed through no fault of yours. Tell us straight away, and we’ll cancel the sale without charging you.']],
 ['s-gst','14. GST',[
  'If you’re GST-registered and selling a business asset, the sale price includes GST and the listing says so. Tell us your ABN when you sign.',
  'So that the buyer’s tax invoice needn’t name you, you and we agree, by this clause, that Subdivision 153-B of the GST Act applies to the sale: we’re treated as making the supply to the buyer and we issue the buyer’s tax invoice in our name, and you’re treated as supplying the vehicle to us at the same price. You don’t issue a tax invoice to the buyer. Your settlement statement shows the GST. You must tell us straight away if your GST registration changes; if either of us isn’t registered when the sale is made, the arrangement doesn’t apply.',
  'GST applies to our seller fee.']],
 ['s-privacy','15. Your information',[
  'We use your details to run the sale. The listing doesn’t name you and shows only your suburb. We give your address, and the directions you’ve given us (who to ask for, the gate), only to a verified member whose viewing we’ve agreed with you and to the buyer whose collection we’ve agreed with you, and we tell you their name first. In Queensland the buyer’s sale statement must name the owner once the vehicle is sold. For the registration transfer, we give you what your part of your state’s form asks for about the buyer, and give the buyer only what their part requires. We check your ID and ownership papers, run PPSR searches, and keep your bank details securely to pay you. See our <a class="blue" href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a>.']],
 ['s-general','16. General',[
  'The Terms of Sale that apply to buyers form part of how we sell your vehicle. If this agreement and those terms conflict about you, this agreement applies.',
  'If your vehicle is in Western Australia, you also sign the vehicle consignment contract the law prescribes there (the Schedule 4 terms of the Motor Vehicle Dealers (Sales) Regulations 1974), and where it differs from this agreement, it applies.',
  'We may update this agreement for future listings. A change doesn’t apply to a vehicle already listed unless you agree to it in writing.',
  'Complaints: contact us first; we acknowledge within 1 business day and aim to resolve within 10 business days, with a review by a manager if you ask. You can also contact your state’s fair trading agency.',
  'We send notices by email, SMS or your seller dashboard, to the details you gave us. Neither of us is responsible for delays caused by events outside reasonable control (see the Terms of Sale, section 17).',
  'If part of this agreement can’t be enforced, it’s read down or left out and the rest still applies.',
  'This agreement is governed by the laws of Queensland, Australia. Nothing in it takes away a protection the law of your own state gives you. Version 15 November 2026.']]
];

export const HELP: [string, string, [string, string][]][] = [
   ['h-start','Getting started',[
    ['Is it free to join?','Yes. Registering, watching and bidding are free. You only pay fees on a vehicle you buy.'],
    ['[[deposit]]What do I need to register?','An email, your legal name, date of birth, home address and an Australian mobile. Before you bid you verify your mobile with an SMS code, verify your ID with a driver licence or passport and a selfie, and pay a refundable bidding deposit by PayID or bank transfer.'],
    ['[[transfer]]What do I need to register?','An email, your legal name, date of birth, home address and an Australian mobile. Before you bid you verify your mobile with an SMS code and your ID with a driver licence or passport and a selfie. No deposit and no card.'],
    ['[[transfer]]Do I need a deposit or a card to bid?','No. Verify your mobile and your ID once and you can bid on anything. If you win, pay by PayID or bank transfer within {{PAY_DAYS}} business days. Buying with finance? Get pre-approved first; your lender can pay us directly.'],
    ['Do I need an app to verify my ID?','No. It all happens in your browser. On a phone, your camera opens for a photo of your licence or passport and a selfie. On a computer, scan the QR code and finish on your phone.'],
    ['Why do you check my ID?','So every bidder (and every seller) is a real, identifiable person. It stops fake bids, protects sellers, and means we release each vehicle only to the right person.'],
    ['I forgot my password.','Tap Sign in, then “Forgot password?”. We’ll email you a reset link.']]],
   ['h-bid','Bidding',[
    ['How does auto-bid work?','Enter the most you’re willing to pay. We bid for you, one increment at a time, only as much as needed to keep you in front, up to your maximum. Nobody else sees your maximum.'],
    ['What are the bid increments?','INCREMENTS'],
    ['What happens when a vehicle is up?','The auctioneer offers it with a short countdown, shown on the page. Every bid near the end resets the countdown so others can answer, so everyone gets a fair go, even on a slow connection. When it runs out (or the auctioneer closes bidding after fair warning), the hammer falls: the highest bid buys it if it meets the reserve.'],
    ['Two people bid the same maximum. Who wins?','Whoever set that maximum first.'],
    ['Can I withdraw a bid?','Yes, until the hammer falls. Withdraw an early bid from the listing any time before the vehicle is offered, or a bid in the live room until the countdown ends; the price is then worked out again without it. Once the hammer falls on your bid, you’ve bought the vehicle. Bidding and withdrawing over and over to move a price isn’t allowed.'],
    ['Will you tell me if I’m outbid?','We text and email you as fast as we can, but delivery isn’t guaranteed. Keep an eye on auctions you care about.'],
    ['What does “reserve not met” mean?','The seller has a minimum price bidding hasn’t reached yet. The seller can lower it until the hammer falls, and the live room shows when it’s been reached (“on the market”). If the hammer falls below it, the vehicle is passed in.'],
    ['What does “passed in” mean?','Bidding didn’t reach the seller’s reserve, so the truck wasn’t sold and nobody owes anything. Unless the seller says no, it goes into a later auction (usually the next one), and its bidders and watchers hear when it’s back. If you were the highest bidder, one of our consultants will be in touch about that auction.'],
    ['Can I buy a truck after the auction?','No. Every truck is sold under the hammer, or not at all: one that’s passed in goes into a later auction, where the seller can lower the reserve. We don’t sell privately in between, and a sale you arrange with an owner you met through us still goes through us.'],
    ['What’s the auction estimate?','Our opinion of where bidding is likely to end, from recent sales of similar trucks and the seller’s photos, video and answers. It’s a guide, not a valuation or a promise: a truck can sell for more or less, or be passed in. The seller’s reserve is never above the low end, and every estimate shows its all-in amounts beside it.'],
    ['Can I ask a question about a truck?','Yes. Use “Ask a question” on the listing. We put it to the owner and reply, and we publish answers that help everyone.'],
    ['I think someone is bidding unfairly.','Use “Report a concern” on any listing. Sellers and their associates can’t bid on their own vehicles.'],
    ['What if the listing is corrected after I bid?','We tell you straight away and show the change on the listing, and the vehicle isn’t offered until at least 24 hours after the change. If it changes your mind, withdraw your bid on the listing.'],
    ['What are fleet sales?','A group of trucks from one seller (a fleet, a council, a company) on one page. In the live auction they’re offered one after another, each as its own lot with its own reserve.'],
    ['How do live auctions work?','Every vehicle is sold in one. At the published start time our licensed auctioneer offers the vehicles one at a time. Join the live room from the sale page or the auction calendar. The first time, you read the auction’s conditions and tick to accept them. Then you see the vehicle that’s up (its photos and the seller’s walkaround video), the current bid, the all-in price and a short countdown, and you bid with one tap. Every bid near the end resets the countdown so others can answer. Can’t be there? Bid early on any vehicle in the sale and we bid for you up to your maximum when it’s offered.'],
    ['Who else is bidding in a live auction?','Other members online, and sometimes registered members bidding in the room or by phone through the auctioneer. Everyone has verified their ID, and every bid goes through the same system.'],
    ['Is there a video of the auction?','No. While a vehicle is up, the room shows its photos and the seller’s walkaround video beside the price and the countdown, and the auctioneer’s calls appear on the page. The price and countdown on the page are what count.'],
    ['Where can I see what’s coming up?','The auction calendar shows every live auction and how many vehicles are in it. You can add it to your phone’s calendar, and bid early on any vehicle in it now.'],
    ['Can I see what vehicles sold for?','Yes. Recently closed results are under Auctions, then Recently closed, and in each live auction’s room. We show the price when a vehicle sold, and “passed in” when it didn’t.']]],
   ['h-deposit','[[deposit]]Bidding deposit',[
    ['What is the bidding deposit?','Money you pay us before you bid, by PayID or bank transfer, so every bidder is serious. It isn’t a fee: it stays yours, it covers every vehicle you’re winning at once, and you can withdraw whatever isn’t holding a bid whenever you like. If you win, the deposit for the price goes towards the vehicle.'],
    ['How much do I need?','{{DEPOSIT_RATE}} of the most you want to bid, at least {{DEPOSIT_MIN}}.{{DEPOSIT_ANY}} For example, a {{DEPOSIT_EG_PAID}} deposit lets you bid up to {{DEPOSIT_EG_LIMIT}}. If you’re winning two vehicles, your deposit needs to cover both. You can top up any time from Account, then Bidding deposit.'],
    ['How do I pay it?','By PayID or bank transfer from an account in your name, quoting your bidder reference (it starts with BID and is shown on your deposit page). PayID usually arrives within a minute; a normal bank transfer can take until the next business day. We text you when it arrives, with your new limit.'],
    ['How do I get my deposit back?','From Account, then Bidding deposit, choose Withdraw. Anything that isn’t holding a bid goes back to the account it came from, usually the same or next business day. If you have a vehicle to pay for, pay for it first.'],
    ['When would I lose my deposit?','Only if you win a vehicle and don’t pay for it. Then we keep the deposit that went towards that vehicle (half goes to the seller for their trouble), and your account may be suspended. The rest of your deposit stays yours. If a sale is cancelled for any other reason, you get it all back.']]],
   ['h-pay','Paying',[
    ['Why don’t you take cards?','A bank transfer can’t be reversed months later the way a card payment can, so sellers know a sale is final, and nobody pays a surcharge. And there are no card details for anyone to steal.'],
    ['[[deposit]]How do I pay for a vehicle I win?','The deposit for the price goes towards it straight away. Pay the balance by PayID or bank transfer within {{PAY_DAYS}} business days, quoting your invoice number. The amount, our account details and (where shown) a single-use PayID are on your invoice page. If your deposit covers the whole invoice, there’s nothing more to pay.'],
    ['[[transfer]]How do I pay for a vehicle I win?','By PayID or bank transfer within {{PAY_DAYS}} business days, quoting your invoice number. The amount, our account details and (where shown) a single-use PayID are on your invoice page. Using finance? Your lender can pay us directly.'],
    ['What fees are added?','A buyer’s premium of {{PREMIUM}} of the price{{PREMIUM_MIN_PART}}, and GST on the premium{{ADMIN_FEE_PART}}. No surcharge, payment fee or transport charge. Every price on the site shows the all-in total beside it, and you see the all-in total again before you confirm a bid. Every estimate shows its all-in amounts too.'],
    ['Is anything added for transport?','No. You collect the truck where it’s kept, so there’s no tow to a yard and nothing for one in our premium. Getting it home is yours to arrange: drive it, or use “Get a transport quote” for a carrier.'],
    ['Can I pay for several vehicles with one transfer?','Yes, with a dealer account (for dealers, fleets and businesses buying several vehicles). Apply in your account with your business name and ABN; once we’ve checked it, your account shows one total and your own payment reference for all your unpaid invoices.'],
    ['Do I get a tax invoice?','Yes. It’s emailed to you as a PDF when you win, and you can download it from your invoice page any time. Add your company name and ABN in your account if you’re buying for a business.'],
    ['[[deposit]]What if I don’t pay?','We remind you first. If you still don’t pay, we cancel the sale, keep the deposit that went towards that vehicle, and close your account for bidding. You can’t open a new one.'],
    ['[[transfer]]What if I don’t pay?','We remind you first. If you still don’t pay, we cancel the sale and close your account for bidding, and you can’t open a new one. There’s no cancellation fee.'],
    ['Do I pay the seller?','Never. You only ever pay Super Trucker. We never change our bank details by email, SMS or phone. If anyone asks you to pay differently, call us on {{PHONE}} first.'],
    ['Can I pay by card, cash or cheque?','No. Only PayID or bank transfer, to the account shown in your account or on your invoice page (or BPAY, where your invoice shows our biller code). Allow up to a business day for a normal transfer to clear; PayID is usually instant.'],
    ['Can I pay by BPAY?','Yes, where your invoice shows our BPAY biller code. Use your own Customer Reference Number (CRN), shown under the bank details: it’s the same every time you pay us, so we know it’s you. BPAY can take a business day or two to reach us, so pay a little before the due date.'],
    ['It’s a big payment. Will my bank let it through?','Check before the auction. Many banks cap PayID and online transfers each day, well below the price of a truck. Raise your limit, or ask your branch for a same-day transfer, so the money can reach us within {{PAY_DAYS}} business days. If it’s on its way and you’ve told us, we won’t cancel a sale over a bank’s processing time.'],
    ['Can someone else pay for me?','Only your lender, if you’re using finance. Otherwise payments must come from an account in your name, or your business’s if you’re buying for it (a joint account you’re named on is fine). We send other payments back to where they came from. It protects you and the seller from fraud.'],
    ['What if I pay late?','We remind you by SMS and email. Overdue balances may attract interest at {{LATE_INTEREST}} a year; there are no other late fees. If you still don’t pay, the sale can be cancelled and your account closed.']]],
   ['h-grade','Visual grades',[
    ['What is the visual grade?','A quick guide to how a vehicle looks in the seller’s photos and video, which we check before it’s listed. We grade paint and body, interior and tyres, plus an overall grade. We don’t grade mechanical condition, because photos and video can’t test it.'],
    ['What does each grade mean?','GRADES'],
    ['Is the grade a guarantee?','No. It’s a guide, like the rest of our report. View the truck, and bring a mechanic if you want a mechanic’s opinion before you bid.']]],
   ['h-collect','Viewing, collection and transfer',[
    ['Where are the trucks?','Where their owners keep them: a yard, a depot, a farm. They stay there from listing to handover. The listing shows the suburb and state. The street address goes only to a verified member with a viewing or collection we’ve booked.'],
    ['Can I see the truck before I bid?','Yes, and we’d encourage it: we’re never at the truck ourselves. Tap “Ask to view it” on the listing and offer up to three times, up to the day before the auction. You need a verified account (the same checks as bidding), because the owner is told who is coming. We agree a time with the owner and text you the address. Bring photo ID, and a mechanic if you like. Every listing also has the owner’s photos and walkaround video, which we check against the papers, the rego and the PPSR search, plus our report and the owner’s written answers.'],
    ['What happens at a viewing?','The owner or their staff show you the truck. Look it over, climb in, start it and hear it run; no road test, and nothing is taken apart. It’s a working yard: closed shoes, follow their rules, stay with your host. Don’t talk price or a private deal: every sale goes through us, and you agree to that when you book. If the owner tells you something that isn’t in the listing and it matters to you, ask us to confirm it in writing before you bid.'],
    ['Can I road test it?','No. You can start it and hear it run at a viewing. If you can’t get there and we have a partner mechanic nearby, you can order an inspection from the listing: the mechanic emails you a written report with photos, and you pay them. Without a hoist a mechanic can’t see everything, and the report says what they could and couldn’t check.'],
    ['Can I deal with the owner directly?','No. You meet the owner at a viewing and at the handover, but every question, offer, payment and problem goes through us. That’s what puts the trust account, the title check and the claims process behind your purchase. If you buy a truck we introduced you to from its owner some other way, you owe us our buyer’s premium anyway (Terms, section 5), and so does the owner, so there’s nothing to save.'],
    ['Is it registered?','Every listing says. Registered trucks show the plate, state and expiry, and you put the registration into your name after you buy. Unregistered trucks are sold without plates: they leave on a carrier or a float, or under a permit.'],
    ['What happens after I pay?','We lodge the seller’s notice of disposal for them, and tell you when it’s ready to collect (straight away if it’s sold unregistered). Book a time from your invoice; we agree it with the seller and send you the address and a 6-digit release code. Putting the registration into your own name is your step, with your own state: your invoice has one button for it, with the form already filled in from your account, and you have the time your state allows (usually 14 days). You don’t need to send us proof, and it never holds up your collection.'],
    ['What if something’s wrong when I get there?','Check the truck against the listing before you give the release code. If something is materially different (new damage, a missing key, parts removed, it no longer starts), don’t give the code: call us from the yard. You choose: go ahead, or cancel the sale for a full refund. Your money is still in our trust account.'],
    ['Who looks after it before I collect?','The seller. It stays in their hands, insured and at their risk, until it’s handed over to you (or from the end of your collection window, if you don’t collect in time). We never have the truck; we hold your money in trust until the handover is done and your claim window has closed.'],
    ['How do I collect?','Book a time from your invoice once we’ve told you it’s ready. We agree it with the seller and send you the address and a 6-digit release code. Collect within {{COLLECT_DAYS}} business days. Check the truck, then give the seller the code: they enter it on our handover page, and it’s yours.'],
    ['Can someone else collect for me?','Yes: a driver or a carrier. Name them when you book. They need photo ID matching that name, and we text them the release code. You’re responsible for them as if they were you.'],
    ['What should I bring to collect?','Photo ID, your release code, and what the truck needs to be moved safely and legally: a driver with the right licence class (the GVM is on the listing), or a carrier. It may be low on fuel or need its batteries charged. The seller doesn’t have to load it or lend equipment. If it’s unregistered, bring a float or your permit.'],
    ['What if I can’t collect in time?','Ask us before the window ends. Otherwise storage of {{STORAGE}} a day applies.'],
    ['Can you deliver?','Use “Get a transport quote” on any listing or on your invoice. An independent carrier quotes from where the truck is kept to your postcode and collects it for you with your release code. Trucks that don’t start go on a float or tilt tray.'],
    ['What does “Starts and drives” mean?','The seller’s video shows it starting and moving under its own power. It isn’t a road test or a mechanical inspection. Other listings say “Starts, but doesn’t drive”, “Doesn’t start” or “Not tested”: allow for a float.']]],
   ['h-returns','Claims and returns',[
    ['Can I return a truck?','Not for change of mind. Trucks are sold as is, where is, and auction purchases have no cooling-off period. View it, read the whole listing and watch the video before you bid.'],
    ['What are my consumer rights?','Every truck is sold by auction, with Super Trucker as the owner’s agent, so you get the guarantees of clear title, undisturbed possession and no undisclosed securities, whoever the seller is. The guarantees about quality don’t apply to sales by auction. If the listing is wrong you can claim, and your rights against misleading descriptions are never affected.'],
    ['Does it come with a warranty?','Any remaining manufacturer’s warranty transfers with the truck. We sell every truck as its owner’s agent and never give a statutory warranty: each listing says so before bidding opens. None applies to an owner’s truck sold at auction in Queensland, New South Wales or Western Australia, and we don’t list a vehicle it could cover. You can arrange an extended warranty or roadside assistance from the partners on our Warranty page; you don’t need one to keep any consumer guarantee rights you have.'],
    ['What if it’s not as described?','If it’s materially different from the listing (wrong year, VIN or transmission, an undisclosed write-off or finance, major damage we didn’t show), lodge a claim from your invoice before handover or within {{CLAIM_DAYS}} business days after. If it’s upheld you can cancel for a full refund.'],
    ['How accurate is your report?','It’s a guide, from the seller’s photos and walkaround video and what the seller declares in writing: we’re never at the truck. It isn’t a mechanical or roadworthy inspection. The facts (VIN, rego, PPSR, GVM, odometer photo, transmission, fuel, listed features, warning lights, damage) are checked by us against the seller’s photos and video and the official records before it’s listed, and the listing shows which parts came from the seller.']]],
   ['h-finance','Finance and insurance',[
    ['Can I get finance?','Yes, through a lender or broker. Use Finance (in the menu) to work out repayments and compare the lenders we work with, then apply with them directly. Get pre-approved before you bid: a bid the hammer falls on is binding, and payment is due when you win. Super Trucker isn’t a lender or credit broker, and we may receive a fee from the lender.'],
    ['Do I need insurance before collecting?','The truck is your responsibility from the handover (or from the end of your collection window if you haven’t collected), and in your name once the registration is transferred. Arrange cover to start at the handover. Insurance (in the menu) compares the insurers we work with. Super Trucker isn’t an insurer and doesn’t give advice; read the PDS and TMD before you buy.'],
    ['Can I get a warranty or roadside assistance?','Yes, from the providers on our Warranty page. Compare what each covers, then ask for a quote. Super Trucker doesn’t sell or recommend warranties, and may receive a commission. Read the PDS or terms before you buy.'],
    ['What happens to my details if I ask a partner to call?','We send the partner named on the form only the details you agree to share, and they contact you about that product. We record your consent. Ask us anytime and we’ll tell the partner to stop.']]],
   ['h-scams','Staying safe',[
    ['How do I know a message is really from Super Trucker?','Our emails come from @{{DOMAIN}} and links go to {{DOMAIN}}. We’ll never ask for your password, sign-in code or bank login, by email, SMS or phone. If a message about a truck, a viewing or a payment doesn’t look right, call us on {{PHONE}} before you act on it.'],
    ['Someone asked me to pay them directly.','Don’t. Only ever pay Super Trucker, using the details on your invoice page. Report it to us on {{PHONE}}.'],
    ['I got an email saying your bank details changed.','That’s a scam. Our bank details never change by email. Call us before you pay anything.'],
    ['Someone I met at a viewing offered to sell me the truck privately.','Say no, and tell us. A private sale has no trust account, title check or claims process behind it, you’d still owe our buyer’s premium (Terms, section 5), and it’s how people lose money on trucks with finance still owing.']]],
   ['h-sell','Selling',[
    ['How does selling work?','Fill in the form on the Sell page (about 10 minutes): type your plate and we fill in the truck, then add the kilometres, its condition, your phone photos, reserve or no reserve, and sign the seller agreement with your finger. We call you within 1 business day with the auction estimate. You then verify your ID, add your bank details and the address it’s kept at, and send us a short walkaround video. We check your photos, video and papers from here (we’re never at your place), write the report, and offer it in our next live auction. Buyers can view it at your place by appointment: we agree each time with you and tell you who’s coming. When it sells and the buyer has paid us, they collect it from you with a release code, and we pay you.'],
    ['Should I get it inspected before it lists?','It often helps. Tick the inspection box when you sign the agreement: a mechanic inspects it, your listing gets an “Inspected” badge and the report, and buyers bid with more confidence. It costs {{PRE_INSPECTION_FEE}} including GST, taken from the sale proceeds only if it sells.'],
    ['Do buyers come to my place?','Yes, by appointment only. We agree every viewing with you first and tell you in writing who is coming; the listing shows your suburb, never your street, and the address goes only to that visitor. They look it over and hear it run: no road test. After the sale, the buyer collects it from you at a time we agree with you. Nobody we haven’t named to you has a booking: turn them away and tell us. If you can’t host viewings, tell us before it’s listed.'],
    ['A visitor wants to buy it from me direct. Can I?','No, and you’d gain nothing. Your agreement makes us your only seller for 90 days, and our buyer’s premium is payable on a sale to anyone we introduced (they’ve agreed to pay it too). Sold through us, the money sits in a trust account until the truck is handed over, any finance is paid out for you, and the buyer can’t come back on you outside our claims process. Tell them to bid, and tell us.'],
    ['What does it cost?','Seller fee: {{SELLER_FEE}}. No charge for checking your photos and video, our report, the PPSR search, or arranging viewings and the handover. There’s no tow to pay for: the buyer collects it from you.'],
    ['Do I have to set a reserve?','No. With no reserve, your vehicle sells to the highest bidder when the auction ends, whatever the price, and no-reserve listings usually attract the most bidders. With a reserve, it only sells at or above that price; it stays secret from bidders, it can’t be above the low end of our estimate, and you can lower it but not raise it once bidding starts.'],
    ['Can I lower my reserve during the auction?','Yes, until the hammer falls: from your seller dashboard (there’s a button to sell at the current bid), or by phoning us while it’s up, when the auctioneer records it for you. It can’t go back up.'],
    ['How is the estimate worked out?','From recent sales of similar vehicles (ours and published results), price guides, and the condition your photos, video and answers show. We agree it with you before the auction and keep a record of what it’s based on. It’s our opinion of where bidding is likely to end, not a promise.'],
    ['Is signing on my phone legally binding?','Yes. Australia’s electronic transactions laws let you sign an agreement like this electronically, by drawing your signature (or typing your name if you can’t draw one). We record the date, time and device, and email you a PDF of exactly what you signed. You confirm it again with your verified ID before the vehicle goes live.'],
    ['What if bidding doesn’t reach my reserve?','It’s passed in: it isn’t sold, and you owe nothing. We offer it again at our next live auction for your state, with no new seller fee, and your consultant calls you first to agree the reserve. Don’t want it offered again? Tell us from your seller dashboard before it’s listed: there’s no fee. To sell it on the day, lower your reserve before the hammer falls: phone us while it’s up and the auctioneer records it. We don’t sell trucks privately after the auction.'],
    ['When do I get paid?','Within {{PAYOUT_DAYS}} business days after you hand it over on the buyer’s release code and their {{CLAIM_DAYS}}-business-day claim window closes, less our fees. If there’s finance owing, we pay your lender first.'],
    ['Do I have to send a video?','Yes: we’re never at the truck, so your walkaround video is how buyers who can’t visit see it run. One per listing, up to 250 MB: start it from cold, film the dash with the engine running, walk slowly around it and through the cab, and move it under its own power if it’s safe where you are. Keep street numbers, street signs, mail, people and other vehicles’ plates out of shot. Add it from your seller dashboard; our team checks it before it appears on the listing, and we remove the location your phone records. A listing has up to 10 photos and videos in total.'],
    ['How do you fill in my vehicle’s details?','From vehicles we’ve listed before, and from the VIN: who made it, where and when, and what other vehicles we’ve listed with a similar VIN are. We don’t buy or copy rego records. Check what we fill in and correct anything that’s wrong.'],
    ['What do I do when it sells?','Once the buyer has paid us in full, we lodge your part of the registration transfer for you, as your agent, and text you when it’s done. The buyer books a time to collect and we agree it with you. On the day: check their photo ID against the name we sent, let them check the truck, then open your handover link and enter their 6-digit release code, the odometer and the keys. Never take money from anyone. If it’s sold without plates, it leaves on a float or under a permit whose number you enter.'],
    ['Can I see who’s bidding?','You can see every bid and its time in your seller dashboard. Bidders’ names are hidden to protect their privacy, and every bidder has verified their mobile and ID.'],
    ['Can I get a report of my vehicles?','Yes. Download it from your seller dashboard (a spreadsheet of every vehicle, its result and your payout). Fleets and businesses selling several vehicles can ask us to group them in one sale page.'],
    ['What if my truck doesn’t sell?','We offer it at a later auction (no extra seller fee), with or without a lower reserve, and your consultant talks it through with you first. Anyone who bid on or watched it last time hears when it’s back.'],
    ['Can I bid on my own truck?','No, and nor can anyone bidding for you. It breaks our agreement, and shill bidding can breach consumer law.']]],
  ];

export const PRIVACY: [string, string][] = [
   ['Who we are','{{LEGAL_NAME}} (ABN {{ABN}}). We handle personal information under the Privacy Act 1988 and the Australian Privacy Principles.'],
   ['What we collect','Buyers: name, date of birth, address, email, mobile, company and ABN if given, the result of your ID check, the name, BSB and account number your deposit and payments come from (so we can match them and send refunds back), bids, offers, purchases, questions and how you use the site. Sellers: the same identity details, plus vehicle ownership papers, answers about the vehicle, finance and lender details, and bank details for your payout.'],
   ['How you use the site','To run and improve Super Trucker we count the pages and app screens viewed, searches (the filters used, such as make, model, price and state, and how many vehicles matched; never the words you type), the type of device, the website or campaign link that brought you, and your approximate state (from your internet connection’s location). We count visits with an anonymous code that changes every day, so we can’t follow a person from one day to the next. We don’t use advertising cookies or sell this information. Browsers that send Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control aren’t counted. Detailed records are deleted after 90 days; only daily totals are kept. When you join, we note where your first visit came from (for example Google or a newsletter link).'],
   ['Why we collect it','To run auctions, verify identity, check ownership and PPSR status, take and make payments, arrange viewings, mechanical inspections and collection, record who we introduced to a vehicle and its owner, prevent fraud and shill bidding, send the alerts you choose, and meet our legal obligations (including record keeping).'],
   ['Who we share it with','A listing doesn’t name the owner or give their street address: it shows the suburb. We give the address where a vehicle is kept, with the owner’s directions, only to a verified member whose viewing we’ve booked and to the buyer whose collection time is confirmed; the owner has agreed to that in their seller agreement. We tell the owner the name of whoever is coming to view or collect, so they know who to expect; the member agrees to that when they book. We never give either side the other’s phone, email or home address. In Queensland, once a vehicle is sold, the buyer’s sale statement names the person who owned it immediately before the sale: section 74 of the Motor Dealers and Chattel Auctioneers Act 2014 and section 8 of its Regulation make us give the buyer that particular, and we can’t contract out of it. For the registration transfer, the seller’s part gets only what the state’s form asks for about the buyer (for example the licence or customer number in New South Wales and Queensland). If you ask a finance, insurance, inspection, transport or warranty partner to contact you, we share the details you agree to with that partner (they’re named on the form), and they may pay us a fee. We also share with our identity-verification provider (Stripe Identity), banking and payments providers (our bank, and our PayID provider when you use a single-use PayID), SMS and email providers (Twilio, Resend), hosting providers (Vercel, Supabase), your lender for a payout, transport providers you book, and authorities where the law requires. Some providers store data outside Australia. In a live auction, the auctioneer and our staff see the name and bidder number of each bidder on the vehicle that’s up, so they can take floor and phone bids and settle disputes; other bidders see only a made-up name.'],
   ['Bank and ID details','We don’t take cards. The bank details your payments come from, and seller bank details and ownership papers, are stored securely, seen only by our team, and used only to match payments, send refunds and pay sellers. ID documents are checked by Stripe Identity; we keep the result, not a copy of your document. If you saved a card with us before we stopped taking cards, it’s held by Stripe, never by Super Trucker.'],
   ['If an account is closed for not paying','We keep a one-way code (a scrambled fingerprint that can’t be turned back into your details) made from the name and date of birth, mobile number and email on the account, so the same person can’t open a new account to bid. We delete it if the decision is reversed.'],
   ['How long we keep it','For as long as your account is open, and afterwards for as long as the law requires for sale and tax records (generally 7 years).'],
   ['Access, correction and deletion','See and update your details in your account, or ask us for a copy of what we hold. You can delete your account yourself, in the app or on the website (Account, then Delete my account), once nothing is in progress (live bids, a purchase not yet paid for and collected, or a vehicle for sale). We then delete your personal details and keep only the sale and tax records the law requires.'],
   ['Our apps','If you allow notifications, we store your phone’s push token, its platform and the app version, so we can send the alerts you choose (you can turn each kind off in the app). The app uses your camera, photos or videos only when you choose to add them to a claim, an appraisal or your listing. We remove the location a phone or camera records from listing photos and videos before they’re published. We don’t use advertising identifiers, track you across other apps or websites, or collect your location.'],
   ['Marketing','We only send marketing (such as our weekly email of new vehicles) if you opt in, under Alerts in your account. Every marketing email and optional alert has a one-click unsubscribe link and our contact details, and we act on an unsubscribe straight away.'],
   ['Complaints','Contact our privacy officer at {{EMAIL}}. If you’re not satisfied, you can contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC).']
  ];

